<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Nov retail sales fall 0.7 pct on year.</title>
<headline>Singapore Nov retail sales fall 0.7 pct on year.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's November retail sales index (base 1991) fell 0.7 percent compared to a year ago, the Department of Statistics said on Sunday.</p>
<p>But the figures showed an improvement of 1.9 percent over October 1996 sales.</p>
<p>Excluding motor vehicles, the index registered a month-on-month rise of 6.0 percent in November.</p>
<p>November retail sales were estimated at Singapore $2.02 billion. The statistics department said that year-on-year, at constant prices, the retail index rose by 0.9 percent.  </p>
<p>				   Month-on-Month     Yr-on-Yr</p>
<p>    Total index		    1.9		 -0.7</p>
<p>    X-vehicle sales		6.0		  6.9</p>
<p>    Textiles/apparels	    1.9		 -0.1</p>
<p>    Furniture/households	22.2		 19.9</p>
<p>    Vehicle sales		-11.5		-22.2</p>
<p>    Petrol stations		2.0		 11.7</p>
<p>    Departments/supermarts     5.9		  3.4</p>
<p>    General provisions	   3.1		  9.8</p>
<p>    Other retail		   3.1		  7.1</p>
</text>
